xternal-link kit-file-line-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a> <a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/SellRoundTripTests.cs" aria-label="tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/SellRoundTripTests.cs on GitHub" data-line="absent" data-comp="file-line-link · primitive · line absent"><span class="kit-file-line-link__text">tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/SellRoundTripTests.cs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-file-line-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a></dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Fix direction</dt><dd>change the start date, amount and address defaults so that none equals the example. (The holder defaults are I10.) Constraints for the new values: (a) Build() stays valid relative to TestClock.Today. The start must sit inside SELL-2's window [2026-10-17, 2026-12-16] but must not be a boundary (today or today+60, which the SELL-2 boundary tests own). It must not be today+15 (2026-11-01, the example start) or today+30 (2026-11-16), because SellTermLengthTests.cs:19-20, :26 and :56 rely on today+30 being a date 'neither the builder defaults nor the api.md example carry'. Today+22 = 2026-11-08, ending 2027-11-07, meets every constraint, for example. (b) The amount must be greater than 0 (SELL-7). It must not be 365.00, and must not equal an amount a test uses as its own value: 412.34 (Distinctive :29, SellTermLengthTests.cs:56, SellPaymentTests.cs:40, :63, SellReferenceTests.cs:70), 389.50 (SellPaymentTests.cs:24), 298.76 (SellRoundTripTests.cs:28), 500.00 (SellReferenceTests.cs:74) or 0.01 (SellAmountTests.cs:25). (c) The address must not be '1 High St' or 'M1 1AA'. It must not be a test's own address either: 7 Canal St/M4 6BX, 22 Mill Lane/M4 5JD, or postcode SW1A 1AA (SellShapeTests.cs:184). The postcode must be 8 characters or fewer. Setting address lines 2 and 3 to non-null values would also stop the example's nulls matching. (d) type, autoRenew and paymentMethod also equal the example (Household, true, DirectDebit), but these are enums and a bool. A default for one of them cannot be stub-proof on its own, because a canned stub can return either value. The skill's parenthetical scope (names, dates, amounts, address) leaves them out. Changing them has consequences, and David should decide. A Cheque default would make every later default renewal a COULD-3 422 (requirements.md:106, 'including a Cheque defaulted under RENEW-3a'). A default of autoRenew false would make later default renewals hit RENEW-3b (the term is unpaid). A Card default would make the 'non-default' Card overrides in SellPaymentTests.cs:34 and :40 no-ops. A BuyToLet/false default would do the same to SellRoundTripTests.cs:56 and Distinctive :27 and :30. Literal expectations that depend on a default that would change: SellPolicyholderCountTests.cs:33 and :55, and SellPaymentTests.cs:44 and :67. Each passes new DateOnly(2027, 10, 31), which is the end for the default start of 2026-11-01. They must take the literal end for the new default start. SoldPolicyAssert reads every other sold value from the request body (SoldPolicyAssert.cs:16-17, :20, :23, :29, :53), so nothing else needs a new literal. Comments that would go stale: SellPolicyRequestBuilder.cs:7-8 ('start 2026-11-01, today + 15') and :23-24 ('the two match'), SellPaymentTests.cs:53-54 ('the default method', if the method changes) and SellRoundTripTests.cs:19-20. Unaffected: Distinctive (:26-36) overrides every field. SellPolicyholderAgeTests sets its own Start = today+15 (:13). SellTermLengthTests.cs:41 sets 2026-11-01 on purpose as the contract row, and once the other defaults change, that row discriminates on everything except the dates.</dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Suggested test</dt><dd><span class="kit-finding-card__absent">not recorded in the excerpt</span></dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Fixed by</dt><dd><span class="kit-finding-card__fix"><span class="kit-sha-link__wrap" data-state="pop"><a class="kit-sha-link__sha kit-sha-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/commit/3070c7b" aria-label="Commit 3070c7b on GitHub">3070c7b<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-sha-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a></span> <span class="kit-sha-link__wrap" data-state="pop"><a class="kit-sha-link__sha kit-sha-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/commit/75421f6" aria-label="Commit 75421f6 on GitHub">75421f6<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-sha-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"></path></svg></a></span><span class="kit-finding-card__trailer">trailer text not in the excerpt</span><span>commit subjects not in the excerpt</span></span></dd></div></dl></article>
