imDateTests.cs:27, :67) and the DataAnnotations 400 rows (ClaimRecordTests.cs:105 description of 501, :112 missing claimDate). Each of these already fails on the stub, because the stub returns a canned 'STUB-CLM' body, persists nothing and never validates, so a 500 just looks like more red. The three claim shape rows that did pass (ClaimRecordTests.cs:122 bad date format, :132 unknown field, :142 malformed JSON) fail inside the System.Text.Json input formatter. The model is never set, so validation never runs and the record check never fires; these rows cannot see the bug by construction. The gate's expectation (loop.jsonl line 4, 'every F3 rule test fails (shape 400s allowed)') reports 10 of 13 F3 _with_400 rows passing. By inference, the two claim DataAnnotations rows above are among the 3 that failed, as 500s. The gate's tolerance for failing rows let that through, because a failing row was acceptable at this step. The detailed per-test output is not in the receipt, so this attribution is inferred, not observed. Only the live curl leg of the stub gate exercises the route outside the red tests, and that is where the bug surfaced.</dd></div><div class="kit-finding-card__field"><dt>Files</dt><dd><a class="kit-file-line-link__link" href="https://github.com/dpmorgandev/uinsure-policies-api/blob/main/tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/ClaimRecordTests.cs" aria-label="tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/ClaimRecordTests.cs on GitHub" data-line="absent" data-comp="file-line-link · primitive · line absent"><span class="kit-file-line-link__text">tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/ClaimRecordTests.cs</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-external-link kit-file-line-link__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 3h6v6"></path><path d="M10 14 21 3"></path><path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-